# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
# wasm/build.sh runs on ubuntu-latest in CI, and bash fails on a CRLF
# script with an opaque "$'\r': command not found".
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the CI workflows themselves and for the Node script
# CI invokes.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf

# Generated artifacts are machine-written; never let them be
# line-ending-normalised, or a rebuild diffs against a mangled copy and
# CI reports drift that isn't there.
#
# Intel HEX in particular: avr-objcopy emits CRLF by convention on every
# platform, so normalising to LF on commit made the committed image
# differ from every fresh build. (avrbro's parser copes with either, so
# this was a false alarm rather than a broken upload -- but a check that
# always fires is a check nobody reads.)
website/app/uti.js -text
*.hex -text
